  <span></span><span class="h">Looking in</span><span class="h">Looking out</span>
  <span class="h rh">From inside the firm</span>
  <div class="cell"><i>1 · Inside-In</i><b>Fix the engine room</b><span>Optimise lines, remove bottlenecks. Misses the geopolitical iceberg: deckchairs on the Titanic.</span></div>
  <div class="cell"><i>2 · Inside-Out</i><b>Watch the supply chain</b><span>Strengthen links to the outside: suppliers, volatile nodes. Better, still not enough for big shocks.</span></div>
  <span class="h rh">From outside the firm</span>
  <div class="cell"><i>3 · Outside-In</i><b>Map what you can't control</b><span>Make external forces visible; spread locations across a portfolio. Still reacts to country-level events.</span></div>
  <div class="cell best"><i>4 · Outside-Out ★ gold standard</i><b>Resilience beyond any one country</b><span>Positions the firm against existential geopolitical threats. Rarely practised in IB.</span></div>
</div>
